Hello, this is Sumanth. Today marks Day 4 of my Cloud Architect journey.

Today’s focus: Networking fundamentals, remote access, DNS resolution, ports, APIs, and troubleshooting.
Date :15-05-2026
Day :Friday

1. ip addr
Purpose: Show network interfaces + IP addresses

Syntax:
ip addr

Example:
ip addr

Output:
inet 192.168.1.25/24


2. hostname -I
Purpose: Show machine IP

Syntax:
hostname -I

Output:
192.168.1.25


3. ping
Purpose: Test connectivity

Syntax:
ping domain

Example:
ping google.com

Output:
64 bytes from google.com


4. traceroute
Purpose: Show packet route

Syntax:
traceroute domain

Example:
traceroute google.com

Output:
hop1
hop2
hop3


5. curl
Purpose: Fetch webpage/API data

Syntax:
curl URL

Example:
curl https://api.github.com

Output:
JSON response


6. wget
Purpose: Download files

Syntax:
wget URL

Example:
wget https://example.com/file.zip

Output:
Downloaded successfully


7. nslookup
Purpose: DNS lookup

Syntax:
nslookup google.com

Output:
IP address result


8. dig
Purpose: Advanced DNS query

Syntax:
dig google.com

Output:
DNS answer section


9. host
Purpose: Quick DNS lookup

Syntax:
host google.com

Output:
google.com has address ...


10. ss -tulnp
Purpose: Show open ports

Syntax:
ss -tulnp

Output:
tcp LISTEN 0 80 nginx


11. netstat -tulnp
Purpose: Legacy port check

Syntax:
netstat -tulnp


12. nc
Purpose: Network testing

Syntax:
nc -zv host port

Example:
nc -zv google.com 443

Output:
Connection successful


13. telnet
Purpose: Port testing

Syntax:
telnet host port

Example:
telnet google.com 80


14. ssh
Purpose: Remote login

Syntax:
ssh user@ip

Example:
ssh ubuntu@192.168.1.100

Output:
Remote shell access


15. ssh-keygen
Purpose: Generate SSH keys

Syntax:
ssh-keygen -t ed25519

Output:
Public/private key created


16. ssh-copy-id
Purpose: Copy SSH key to server

Syntax:
ssh-copy-id user@server


17. scp
Purpose: Secure file copy

Syntax:
scp source user@server:path

Example:
scp app.zip ubuntu@server:/home/ubuntu


18. rsync
Purpose: Efficient sync

Syntax:
rsync -av source destination

Example:
rsync -av project/ backup/


19. Route check

ip route

Output:
default via 192.168.1.1


20. DNS config

cat /etc/resolv.conf


21. Public IP

curl ifconfig.me


22. HTTP request headers

curl -I https://google.com


23. HTTP methods

GET
POST
PUT
DELETE


24. API GET example

curl https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/1


25. API POST example

curl -X POST https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{"title":"cloud"}'


26. JSON formatting

curl api_url | jq


27. Install jq

sudo apt install jq


28. OpenSSL test

openssl s_client -connect google.com:443


29. Firewall check

sudo ufw status


30. Enable firewall

sudo ufw enable


31. Allow SSH

sudo ufw allow 22


32. Allow HTTP

sudo ufw allow 80


33. Allow HTTPS

sudo ufw allow 443


34. Common Ports

22 SSH
53 DNS
80 HTTP
443 HTTPS
3306 MySQL
5432 PostgreSQL
6379 Redis
27017 MongoDB


35. OSI Layers

1 Physical
2 Data Link
3 Network
4 Transport
5 Session
6 Presentation
7 Application


36. TCP vs UDP

TCP = reliable
UDP = faster


37. HTTP Status Codes

200 OK
301 Redirect
400 Bad Request
401 Unauthorized
403 Forbidden
